  "title": "EU and China Limit Hybrid Vehicle Imports",
  "summary": "The European Commission has confirmed a new import limit of 350,000 hybrid electric vehicles (HEVs) from China a year, halving the market share to 3% as per the EU’s WTO rules. This move aims to address concerns about energy security and trade tensions. The deal marks a significant step in balancing European and Chinese interests in the automotive sector.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The European Commission confirmed a new import limit of 350,000 hybrid electric vehicles (HEVs) from China a year.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Imports have been soaring in the past two years; about 800,000 battery and plug-in hybrids are likely to be sold this year.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The EU is to limit the number of hybrid electric vehicles imported from China to 350,000 cars a year, the European Commission has confirmed.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
