      "title": "EU to limit Chinese hybrid vehicle imports to 350,000 a year",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/12/eu-deal-china-limit-imports-hybrid-electric-vehicles",
      "description": "<p>Brussels uses WTO rules to quickly impose quota, which will halve Chinese market share to 3%</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2026/oct/12/uk-growth-inflation-pressures-oil-price-sveriges-riksbank-nobel-prize-economic-sciences-awarded-latest-news-updates\">Business live – latest updates</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/11/volkswagen-boss-backs-eu-plan-to-boost-domestic-european-industry\">VW boss backs EU plan to bolster domestic industry</a></p></li></ul><p>The EU is to limit the number of hybrid electric vehicles imported from China to 350,000 cars a year, the European Commission has confirmed.</p><p>Imports have been soaring in the past two years; about 800,000 battery and plug-in hybrids are likely to be sold this year.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/12/eu-deal-china-limit-imports-hybrid-electric-vehicles\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-12T11:23:55"
    },
    {
      "title": "Stellantis and Renault back UK to get EU car industry protection",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/12/stellantis-renault-uk-eu-car-industry-imports-china",
      "description": "<p>Bosses of Citroën owner and French carmaker also urge UK government to consider limiting imports from China</p><p>Stellantis and Renault have backed the UK car industry for inclusion in proposed rules to protect EU industry, but urged the British government to consider limiting imports of Chinese cars.</p><p>Emanuele Cappellano, who leads Stellantis’s European brands including Fiat, Citroën, Opel and Vauxhall, and François Provost, the chief executive of France’s Renault, said the UK should effectively be counted as one of the EU’s 27 member states for the purposes of the proposed <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/16/made-in-europe-laws-could-derail-uk-eu-reset-plans\">“Made in Europe” legislation</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/12/stellantis-renault-uk-eu-car-industry-imports-china\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
